 \subsection*{Part C. Inpact of PH on enzyme activity}
	\begin{steps}
        \newstep[] In the following you will measure enzyme activity at different PH.
     \newstep[] Find three new jumbo test tubes with stoppers and label them as A3, and A4. With a clean Morh's pipette, pipette 5mL of the 0.04\% starch solution into test tubes A3, and A4. Make sure your Morh's pipette is clean. 
     
    \newstep[] Add 1 drops of \ce{HCl} to test tube A3. Close the test tube with a stopper, and mix well its content by inverting the test tube 3 times at constant speed. Measure its PH using PH paper and write down the value in the results section. Make sure the PH is at least one PH unit different than the reference PH. If its not, add more acid until you achieve this difference. Write down this PH in the results section.
        \newstep[] Add 1 drops of \ce{NaOH} to test tube A4. Close the test tube with a stopper, and mix well its content by inverting the test tube 3 times at constant speed. Measure its PH using PH paper and write down the value in the results section. Make sure the PH is at least one PH unit different than the reference PH. If its not, add more base until you achieve this difference. Write down this PH in the results section.
 
 
   \newstep[] Pipette 3mL from test tube A3 into a clean cuvette. Using the plastic dropper, add one drop of the enzyme solution. Very quicly, take small parafilm square and pull tight over top of cuvette hold with thumb and invert once to mix. Start measuring the absorbances and start counting time. 
         \newstep[] Measure absorbance every 15 seconds for two minutes. Write down the results in the results section.
 
         
         
         
         \newstep[] Repeat the previous two steps for test tube A4.
         \end{steps}


 \subsection*{Part D. Inpact of \ce{AgNO3} on enzyme activity}
	\begin{steps}
        \newstep[] In the following you will measure enzyme activity in the presence of \ce{AgNO3}.
     \newstep[] Find a new jumbo test tube with a stopper and label it as A5. With a clean Morh's pipette, pipette 5mL of the 0.04\% starch solution into test the tube. Make sure your Morh's pipette is clean. 
     
    \newstep[] Add 1 drops of the \ce{AgNO3} solution to the test tube. Close the test tube with a stopper, and mix well its content by inverting the test tube 3 times at constant speed. 
           
             \newstep[] Pipette 3mL from test tube A5 into a clean cuvette. Using the plastic dropper, add one drop of the enzyme solution. Very quicly, take small parafilm square and pull tight over top of cuvette hold with thumb and invert once to mix. Start measuring the absorbances and start counting time. 
         \newstep[] Measure absorbance every 15 seconds for two minutes. Write down the results in the results section.
           
         \end{steps}


      
      
   
